## ❤️ RMSSD Logic: The "Missing Link"
*Why did the previous run have an MAE of 1.1?*

Arousal in physiological signals is not captured by "Average BPM" alone. It is captured by **Heart Rate Variability (HRV)**. 
- **BPM (V1 Data):** Only tells you if the heart is fast or slow. Too generic for 1-9 emotion scales.
- **RMSSD (V2 Data):** Measures the *Successive Differences* between beats. 
- **The "47 Samples":** Our 47-second windows (1Hz sampling) allow us to calculate RMSSD for each clip. This variability is the direct indicator of the autonomic response to emotion.

